# Unified restaurant menu (GLOBAL RULE)

There is **ONE** canonical menu in Supabase (`categories`, `products`, modifiers, variants).

**Admin Menu CMS** is the management UI for that data. All consumer interfaces read the **same** rows:

- Admin Menu CMS (via `/api/admin/catalog`, mutations → `menu-catalog-service`)
- Public website menu (`/api/menu`, `useMenuCatalog`)
- QR table menu (`/api/menu`, `QrTableMenuProvider`)
- POS / waiter / server / cashier / delivery (all via `/api/menu` or `menu-catalog-service`)

## Required patterns

- **Read menu (customer/staff ordering):** `GET /api/menu` or server helpers:
  - `getActiveCategories()` / `getActiveProducts()` from `@/lib/menu/menu-catalog-service`
  - Visibility: `@/lib/menu/menu-visibility` (`isCategoryVisibleForMenu`, `isProductListedInCatalog`)
- **Admin mutations:** `/api/admin/categories`, `/api/admin/products` → call `invalidateMenuCache()` after every change
- **Safe delete:** `deleteCategorySafe()` / `deleteProductSafe()` — never hard-delete when order history exists
- **QR nav:** `buildQrCategoryNavItemsFromDb(categories)` — never hardcoded category slug lists

## Forbidden

- QR-only / website-only / POS-only category or product arrays
- Hardcoded product lists or category order in frontend
- Static JSON menu files used at runtime
- `mergeTajineHauptgerichteCatalog` or any fallback that injects products not in Supabase
- Local caches that survive Admin delete (must invalidate + refetch on realtime `menu` scope)
- Separate Supabase queries with **different** visibility filters per page (use shared service)

## UI-only exceptions (NOT menu data)

- `ADMIN_MENU_SECTIONS` — section taxonomy labels (food/drinks/desserts/special) for admin grouping
- `QR_VIRTUAL_NAV_GROUPS` — virtual QR pages (`hot-drinks`, `cold-drinks`, `desserts`) driven by `categories.nav_group` in DB
- Layout/branding differences between QR, website, and POS are allowed

## After any Admin menu change

Must propagate without redeploy: DB update → `invalidateMenuCache()` → Supabase realtime on `categories`/`products` → clients refetch `/api/menu`.
